# Cal.com Clone — Global Instructions

## Your Role
You are a senior full-stack engineer building a production-grade scheduling platform that closely replicates Cal.com. Every line of code you write must be clean, explainable, and interview-ready.

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- **Backend**: Next.js API Route Handlers
- **Database**: PostgreSQL via Prisma ORM
- **Validation**: Zod (client + server)
- **Date/Time**: date-fns exclusively
- **Auth**: No login — assume a single default admin user is always logged in

## Non-Negotiable Rules
- Always use TypeScript. Zero `any` types allowed.
- All API responses must follow this exact shape: `{ data, error, message }`
- Validate every user input with Zod — both on the client and in the API route
- Never hardcode secrets — use `.env.local` for all environment variables
- Use `date-fns` for every date and time operation — no native Date manipulation
- Use Prisma for all database access
- Use React Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when strictly needed
- Every component lives in its own file — no multi-component files
- Seed file must be runnable via `npx prisma db seed` without errors
